    "contentEn": "Ms Wong owns Ocean Café as a sole proprietor. The following information relates to 31 December 2026:\nRenovation (cost) \\$80,000; accumulated depreciation \\$32,000\nKitchen equipment (cost) \\$45,000; accumulated depreciation \\$13,500\nInventory \\$7,200\nPrepaid insurance \\$1,800\nCash at bank \\$14,300\nCash in hand \\$2,200\nTrade payables \\$9,600\nAccrued wages \\$4,200\nBank loan \\$60,000 (\\$12,000 is repayable during 2027; the rest in instalments from 2028 to 2031)\nCapital (1 January 2026) \\$30,000\nAdditional cash capital introduced by Ms Wong during the year \\$10,000\nProfit for the year \\$8,600\nDrawings: cash \\$15,000; goods costing \\$2,400 taken for own use\n(a) State how the bank loan should be classified in the statement of financial position, with the amount of each part.\n(b) Prepare the statement of financial position of Ocean Café as at 31 December 2026.\n(c) Calculate the working capital, comment on the café's ability to meet its short-term obligations, and suggest two ways to improve it.",
    "explanationEn": "This tests three points that are often mishandled: one loan split into current and non-current parts by repayment date; additional capital shown separately in the capital section; and drawings that include goods taken by the owner. Working capital in (c) is negative, and the answer must explain what that means for this business rather than recite a general conclusion.",
    "markingScheme": "（a）2 分：流動部分及金額 1 分；非流動部分及金額 1 分。\n（b）9 分：兩項非流動資產以淨值列示 2 分；流動資產 2 分；流動負債包括貸款一年內到期部分 2 分；資本部分列出額外注入資本 1 分及提用含貨品 1 分；總額相等 1 分。\n（c）5 分：營運資金計算 1 分；解釋負數的含意 1 分；結合本題資料評論 1 分；兩項改善方法各 1 分。\n建議用時 24 分鐘。\n本題所列分數為本平台練習用尺度，並非香港考試及評核局的分數分配。參考答案列出必達步驟與數字，交卷後請逐項對照自評，機器不會為本題評分。",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) 2 marks: current part with amount 1; non-current part with amount 1.\n(b) 9 marks: both non-current assets at net book value 2; current assets 2; current liabilities including the current portion of the loan 2; capital section showing additional capital 1 and drawings including goods 1; totals agree 1.\n(c) 5 marks: working capital 1; meaning of a negative figure 1; comment using this case's data 1; two ways to improve, 1 each.\nSuggested time: 24 minutes.\nThe marks shown are a practice scale used on this platform, not an HKEAA mark allocation. The reference answer lists the required steps and figures. Compare your own work against it point by point; nothing here is machine-marked.",
    "suggestedMinutes": 24
