    "difficulty": "medium",
    "year": 0,
    "content": "青衣五金行為獨資商店。截至 2026 年 12 月 31 日止年度的資料如下：\n銷貨 \\$480,000\n銷貨退回 \\$6,000\n存貨（2026 年 1 月 1 日）\\$42,000\n購貨 \\$318,000\n購貨退出 \\$4,500\n進貨運費 \\$3,500\n存貨（2026 年 12 月 31 日）\\$51,000\n租金 \\$72,000\n工資 \\$54,000\n水電費 \\$9,800\n送貨運費 \\$4,200\n設備折舊 \\$6,000\n已收佣金 \\$3,000\n（a）計算銷貨成本。\n（b）編製青衣五金行截至 2026 年 12 月 31 日止年度的收益表。\n（c）解釋為何進貨運費計入銷貨成本，而送貨運費則列作費用。",
    "explanation": "本題考核收益表的兩個層次：先以淨銷貨減銷貨成本得出毛利，再加其他收入、減各項費用得出淨利。計算淨購貨時須減購貨退出、加進貨運費。常見錯誤是把送貨運費計入銷貨成本，或忘記從銷貨中扣除銷貨退回。",
    "referenceAnswer": "（a）淨購貨 = \\$318,000 − \\$4,500 + \\$3,500 = \\$317,000；銷貨成本 = \\$42,000 + \\$317,000 − \\$51,000 = \\$308,000。\n（b）青衣五金行收益表（截至 2026 年 12 月 31 日止年度）\n銷貨 \\$480,000，減銷貨退回 \\$6,000，淨銷貨 \\$474,000\n銷貨成本：期初存貨 \\$42,000，加淨購貨 \\$317,000，可供銷售貨品 \\$359,000，減期末存貨 \\$51,000，銷貨成本 \\$308,000\n毛利 \\$166,000\n加：已收佣金 \\$3,000，合計 \\$169,000\n減：費用 —— 租金 \\$72,000；工資 \\$54,000；水電費 \\$9,800；送貨運費 \\$4,200；設備折舊 \\$6,000；費用合計 \\$146,000\n本年度淨利 \\$23,000\n（c）進貨運費是把貨品運到店舖、使其可供出售所必須的成本，屬購入貨品成本的一部分，故計入銷貨成本並影響毛利。送貨運費是把已售貨品送交顧客的分銷開支，於銷售之後才發生，故列作費用，只影響淨利。",
    "marks": 12,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) Net purchases = \\$318,000 − \\$4,500 + \\$3,500 = \\$317,000; cost of goods sold = \\$42,000 + \\$317,000 − \\$51,000 = \\$308,000.\n(b) Tsing Yi Hardware — Income statement for the year ended 31 December 2026\nSales \\$480,000, less returns inwards \\$6,000, net sales \\$474,000\nCost of goods sold: opening inventory \\$42,000, add net purchases \\$317,000, goods available for sale \\$359,000, less closing inventory \\$51,000, cost of goods sold \\$308,000\nGross profit \\$166,000\nAdd: commission received \\$3,000, total \\$169,000\nLess expenses: rent \\$72,000; wages \\$54,000; utilities \\$9,800; carriage outwards \\$4,200; depreciation of equipment \\$6,000; total expenses \\$146,000\nProfit for the year \\$23,000\n(c) Carriage inwards is a necessary cost of getting goods to the shop ready for sale, so it is part of the cost of purchases and affects gross profit. Carriage outwards is a distribution cost of delivering goods already sold to customers; it arises after the sale, so it is an expense and affects only profit for the year.",
    "contentEn": "Tsing Yi Hardware is a sole proprietorship. Information for the year ended 31 December 2026:\nSales \\$480,000\nReturns inwards \\$6,000\nInventory (1 January 2026) \\$42,000\nPurchases \\$318,000\nReturns outwards \\$4,500\nCarriage inwards \\$3,500\nInventory (31 December 2026) \\$51,000\nRent \\$72,000\nWages \\$54,000\nUtilities \\$9,800\nCarriage outwards \\$4,200\nDepreciation of equipment \\$6,000\nCommission received \\$3,000\n(a) Calculate the cost of goods sold.\n(b) Prepare the income statement of Tsing Yi Hardware for the year ended 31 December 2026.\n(c) Explain why carriage inwards is part of cost of goods sold while carriage outwards is an expense.",
    "explanationEn": "This tests the two levels of an income statement: net sales less cost of goods sold gives gross profit; other income added and expenses deducted give profit for the year. Net purchases deduct returns outwards and add carriage inwards. Common errors are putting carriage outwards into cost of goods sold, or not deducting returns inwards from sales.",
    "markingScheme": "（a）3 分：淨購貨 2 分（購貨退出 1 分、進貨運費 1 分）；銷貨成本 1 分。\n（b）7 分：淨銷貨 1 分；銷貨成本部分 1 分；毛利 1 分；其他收入 1 分；費用項目完整 2 分；淨利 1 分。\n（c）2 分：兩項運費各 1 分，須說明其與毛利或淨利的關係。\n建議用時 18 分鐘。\n本題所列分數為本平台練習用尺度，並非香港考試及評核局的分數分配。參考答案列出必達步驟與數字，交卷後請逐項對照自評，機器不會為本題評分。",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) 3 marks: net purchases 2 (returns outwards 1, carriage inwards 1); cost of goods sold 1.\n(b) 7 marks: net sales 1; cost of goods sold section 1; gross profit 1; other income 1; complete expenses 2; profit 1.\n(c) 2 marks: 1 for each type of carriage, linked to gross profit or profit for the year.\nSuggested time: 18 minutes.\nThe marks shown are a practice scale used on this platform, not an HKEAA mark allocation. The reference answer lists the required steps and figures. Compare your own work against it point by point; nothing here is machine-marked.",
    "suggestedMinutes": 18
