    "difficulty": "hard",
    "year": 0,
    "content": "將軍澳文具批發由東主郭先生獨資經營。以下資料摘自截至 2026 年 12 月 31 日止年度的試算表：\n銷貨 \\$620,000\n銷貨退回 \\$8,000\n存貨（2026 年 1 月 1 日）\\$55,000\n購貨 \\$402,000\n租金 \\$66,000\n工資 \\$88,000\n保險 \\$12,000\n壞賬 \\$2,500\n呆賬準備（2026 年 1 月 1 日）\\$3,000\n應收賬款 \\$90,000\n汽車（成本）\\$150,000\n汽車累計折舊（2026 年 1 月 1 日）\\$54,000\n雜項費用 \\$5,300\n附註：\n1. 2026 年 12 月 31 日的存貨為 \\$61,000。\n2. 郭先生年內取去成本 \\$3,000 的貨品自用，尚未入賬。\n3. 已付租金中 \\$6,000 屬 2027 年 1 月的租金。\n4. 2026 年 12 月的工資 \\$8,000 尚未支付。\n5. 呆賬準備須調整至應收賬款的 5%。\n6. 汽車以餘額遞減法按 20% 折舊。\n（a）計算經調整後的：(i) 租金；(ii) 工資；(iii) 呆賬準備的增加額；(iv) 本年度汽車折舊。\n（b）編製將軍澳文具批發截至 2026 年 12 月 31 日止年度的收益表。\n（c）解釋東主取去自用的貨品為何以成本從購貨中扣除，而不當作銷貨入賬。",
    "explanation": "本題把多項期末調整集中在同一張收益表：預付租金減少本年費用、應計工資增加本年費用、呆賬準備只把增加額列作費用、餘額遞減法以賬面淨值計算折舊，而東主自用貨品須先從購貨中扣除。任何一項處理錯誤都會令淨利出錯，故須逐項寫出計算。",
    "referenceAnswer": "（a）(i) 租金 = \\$66,000 − \\$6,000 = \\$60,000\n(ii) 工資 = \\$88,000 + \\$8,000 = \\$96,000\n(iii) 期末呆賬準備 = \\$90,000 × 5% = \\$4,500；增加額 = \\$4,500 − \\$3,000 = \\$1,500\n(iv) 折舊 = (\\$150,000 − \\$54,000) × 20% = \\$19,200\n（b）將軍澳文具批發收益表（截至 2026 年 12 月 31 日止年度）\n銷貨 \\$620,000，減銷貨退回 \\$8,000，淨銷貨 \\$612,000\n銷貨成本：期初存貨 \\$55,000，加購貨 \\$402,000 減自用貨品 \\$3,000 即 \\$399,000，可供銷售貨品 \\$454,000，減期末存貨 \\$61,000，銷貨成本 \\$393,000\n毛利 \\$219,000\n減：費用 —— 租金 \\$60,000；工資 \\$96,000；保險 \\$12,000；壞賬 \\$2,500；呆賬準備增加 \\$1,500；汽車折舊 \\$19,200；雜項費用 \\$5,300；費用合計 \\$196,500\n本年度淨利 \\$22,500\n（c）東主取去貨品並非與顧客進行的交易，企業沒有因此取得收入；這是東主從企業提取資源，性質屬提用。以成本入賬（借：提用；貸：購貨），可避免在沒有銷售的情況下虛增收入及毛利，並使銷貨成本只反映真正為銷售而耗用的貨品。",
    "marks": 16,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) (i) Rent = \\$66,000 − \\$6,000 = \\$60,000\n(ii) Wages = \\$88,000 + \\$8,000 = \\$96,000\n(iii) Closing allowance = \\$90,000 × 5% = \\$4,500; increase = \\$4,500 − \\$3,000 = \\$1,500\n(iv) Depreciation = (\\$150,000 − \\$54,000) × 20% = \\$19,200\n(b) Tseung Kwan O Stationery Wholesale — Income statement for the year ended 31 December 2026\nSales \\$620,000, less returns inwards \\$8,000, net sales \\$612,000\nCost of goods sold: opening inventory \\$55,000, add purchases \\$402,000 less goods for own use \\$3,000 = \\$399,000, goods available for sale \\$454,000, less closing inventory \\$61,000, cost of goods sold \\$393,000\nGross profit \\$219,000\nLess expenses: rent \\$60,000; wages \\$96,000; insurance \\$12,000; bad debts \\$2,500; increase in allowance for doubtful accounts \\$1,500; depreciation of motor vehicle \\$19,200; sundry expenses \\$5,300; total expenses \\$196,500\nProfit for the year \\$22,500\n(c) Goods taken by the owner are not a transaction with a customer and bring the business no revenue; the owner is withdrawing resources, which is drawings. Recording them at cost (debit drawings, credit purchases) avoids overstating revenue and gross profit when nothing was sold, and keeps cost of goods sold to the goods actually used up in making sales.",
    "contentEn": "Mr Kwok owns Tseung Kwan O Stationery Wholesale as a sole proprietor. The following is taken from the trial balance for the year ended 31 December 2026:\nSales \\$620,000\nReturns inwards \\$8,000\nInventory (1 January 2026) \\$55,000\nPurchases \\$402,000\nRent \\$66,000\nWages \\$88,000\nInsurance \\$12,000\nBad debts \\$2,500\nAllowance for doubtful accounts (1 January 2026) \\$3,000\nTrade receivables \\$90,000\nMotor vehicle (cost) \\$150,000\nAccumulated depreciation on motor vehicle (1 January 2026) \\$54,000\nSundry expenses \\$5,300\nNotes:\n1. Inventory at 31 December 2026 was \\$61,000.\n2. During the year Mr Kwok took goods costing \\$3,000 for his own use; this has not been recorded.\n3. \\$6,000 of the rent paid relates to January 2027.\n4. Wages of \\$8,000 for December 2026 are unpaid.\n5. The allowance for doubtful accounts is to be adjusted to 5% of trade receivables.\n6. The motor vehicle is depreciated at 20% per year, reducing-balance method.\n(a) Calculate the adjusted: (i) rent; (ii) wages; (iii) increase in the allowance for doubtful accounts; (iv) depreciation of the motor vehicle for the year.\n(b) Prepare the income statement of Tseung Kwan O Stationery Wholesale for the year ended 31 December 2026.\n(c) Explain why goods taken by the owner are deducted from purchases at cost rather than recorded as sales.",
    "explanationEn": "This brings several period-end adjustments into one income statement: prepaid rent reduces the year's expense, accrued wages increase it, only the increase in the allowance is charged, reducing-balance depreciation is based on net book value, and goods taken by the owner are first deducted from purchases. Any one mistake changes the profit, so each working should be shown.",
    "markingScheme": "（a）6 分：租金 1 分；工資 1 分；呆賬準備增加額 2 分（期末準備 1 分、增加額 1 分）；折舊 2 分（賬面淨值 1 分、答案 1 分）。\n（b）8 分：淨銷貨 1 分；購貨扣除自用貨品 1 分；銷貨成本 1 分；毛利 1 分；費用項目完整並採用經調整數字 3 分；淨利 1 分。\n（c）2 分：指出性質屬提用而非銷售 1 分；說明以成本入賬的原因 1 分。\n建議用時 24 分鐘。\n本題所列分數為本平台練習用尺度，並非香港考試及評核局的分數分配。參考答案列出必達步驟與數字，交卷後請逐項對照自評，機器不會為本題評分。",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) 6 marks: rent 1; wages 1; increase in allowance 2 (closing allowance 1, increase 1); depreciation 2 (net book value 1, answer 1).\n(b) 8 marks: net sales 1; purchases less goods for own use 1; cost of goods sold 1; gross profit 1; complete expenses using adjusted figures 3; profit for the year 1.\n(c) 2 marks: drawings, not a sale 1; reason for recording at cost 1.\nSuggested time: 24 minutes.\nThe marks shown are a practice scale used on this platform, not an HKEAA mark allocation. The reference answer lists the required steps and figures. Compare your own work against it point by point; nothing here is machine-marked.",
    "suggestedMinutes": 24
